WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.773
Maggie gasped. "Oh my gosh," she said. "You're right, Henry!

2
00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:15.437
I forgot that Nathan and Nora were only wearing bathing suits when they stopped at the lemonade stand."

3
00:00:15.438 --> 00:00:17.644
"Me too," Cole said.

4
00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:20.651
"But I remember now," Maggie went on.

5
00:00:20.652 --> 00:00:25.590
"Nathan dripped all over my shoes while I was talking to him."

6
00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:29.767
"Sorry about that," Nathan said sheepishly.

7
00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:34.521
"We forgot to bring towels to the pool. Good thing it was a hot day."

8
00:00:34.522 --> 00:00:39.945
"That's why you had to borrow money to buy lemonade, right?" Henry said.

9
00:00:39.946 --> 00:00:46.371
Nathan nodded. "We didn't bring anything with us to the pool," he said.

10
00:00:46.372 --> 00:00:51.068
"But Mrs. Martin let us borrow enough money to buy two cups of lemonade."

11
00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:55.429
"So you guys really didn't take my money?" Maggie asked.

12
00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.959
She sounded kind of disappointed.

13
00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.992
"You said yourself there was lots of money in your cashbox," Cole said to Maggie.

14
00:01:02.993 --> 00:01:06.382
"Was there too much for Nora to hide in her hands?"

15
00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:09.011
"Definitely," Maggie said.

16
00:01:09.012 --> 00:01:13.458
"There were a bunch of dollar bills and lots of change too.

17
00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:17.027
Way too much for anyone to hide in their hands."

18
00:01:17.028 --> 00:01:23.329
"I guess that proves it," Henry said. "Nathan and Nora couldn't have done it."

19
00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:28.025
"Yeah," Cole added. "Sorry we accused you guys."

20
00:01:28.026 --> 00:01:31.862
"It's all right," Nathan said with a smile.

21
00:01:31.863 --> 00:01:36.496
"Cool," Henry said, glad that Nathan wasn't angry.

22
00:01:36.497 --> 00:01:40.495
"Sorry I took the extra lemonade, Maggie," Nora said.

23
00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:44.121
"I was just really thirsty after swimming."

24
00:01:44.122 --> 00:01:47.445
"That's okay," Maggie told the younger girl.

25
00:01:47.446 --> 00:01:51.411
"But please remember to ask next time, okay?"

26
00:01:51.412 --> 00:01:54.399
"I promise!" Nora said.

27
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.697
"So now what?" Cole shrugged. "Nora and Nathan didn't take the money.

28
00:01:59.698 --> 00:02:04.168
Those two teenage girls didn't do it either. Neither did Ryan."

29
00:02:04.169 --> 00:02:08.631
Cole stared at Henry and Maggie. They stared back.

30
00:02:08.632 --> 00:02:12.443
Henry knew they were all thinking the same thing.

31
00:02:12.444 --> 00:02:18.250
"So who did it?" he asked. "We're all out of suspects."

32
00:02:18.251 --> 00:02:23.154
"No, we're not," Maggie said. "What about Mrs. Martin?

33
00:02:23.155 --> 00:02:26.559
She was hanging around when the cash went missing."

34
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.684
"Mrs. Martin?" Cole said. "We already talked about that, remember?

35
00:02:31.685 --> 00:02:35.458
She couldn't be the thief. She's a police officer."

36
00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:38.466
Nora wasn't paying attention anymore.

37
00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:43.898
She and her friend were already back to arguing about who was a better princess.

38
00:02:43.899 --> 00:02:47.294
But Nathan was still listening to Henry and his friends.

39
00:02:47.295 --> 00:02:51.067
"Not right now she isn't," he pointed out.

40
00:02:51.068 --> 00:02:54.816
"Mrs. Martin took time off from the police force.

41
00:02:54.817 --> 00:02:58.269
She's going back to work when Marty gets a little older."

42
00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:02.416
"I forgot about that!" Maggie exclaimed.

43
00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:06.393
"Me too, but that's not the point," Henry said.

44
00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:10.041
"Mrs. Martin is an honest person and a mother.

45
00:03:10.042 --> 00:03:14.459
She wouldn't steal money, especially not from a kid."

46
00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.871
"How do we know that for sure?" Maggie said.

47
00:03:17.872 --> 00:03:22.259
"What if she's short of cash right now since she isn't working?"

48
00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:27.051
"Don't be silly," Cole said. "Mr. Martin still has a job.

49
00:03:27.052 --> 00:03:29.327
He's a teacher at the college."

50
00:03:29.328 --> 00:03:32.912
"But what if he doesn't make enough money?" Maggie said.

51
00:03:32.913 --> 00:03:38.021
"They used to have two salaries to pay the bills, and now they only have one.

52
00:03:38.022 --> 00:03:42.430
Plus they have a kid who's growing and needs stuff all the time."

53
00:03:42.431 --> 00:03:45.410
She stared around at all of them.

54
00:03:45.411 --> 00:03:49.591
"Maybe they barely have enough to get by, and she's desperate.

55
00:03:49.592 --> 00:03:53.063
Desperate enough to steal any money she can find!"

56
00:03:53.064 --> 00:04:00.364
Henry sighed. "That sounds more like something from a movie than real life, Maggie."

57
00:04:00.365 --> 00:04:05.534
"Besides I don't think Mrs. Martin is that desperate," Nathan added.

58
00:04:05.535 --> 00:04:09.512
"She bought lemonade for Nora and me, remember?

59
00:04:09.513 --> 00:04:14.085
Plus she bought two cups for herself and one for Marty."

60
00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:19.335
"Marty?" Nora looked up suddenly at the sound of Marty's name.

61
00:04:19.336 --> 00:04:24.366
"Yuck! I don't like Marty Martin one bit!"

62
00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:30.742
Maggie, Nathan, and Cole didn't even look over at her. But Henry did.

63
00:04:30.743 --> 00:04:36.626
"What do you mean, Nora?" he asked. "Why don't you like Marty Martin?"

64
00:04:36.627 --> 00:04:38.794
Nora scowled.

65
00:04:38.795 --> 00:04:46.236
"When my mom babysits him at our house, he's always grabbing my stuff and saying it's his," she complained.

66
00:04:46.237 --> 00:04:51.695
"He even tried to take my microphone so I couldn't play rock star anymore!"

67
00:04:51.696 --> 00:04:56.555
"No way!" her friend cried. "That's mean!"

68
00:04:56.556 --> 00:05:02.741
Henry hardly heard the other little girl. "That's it!" he cried.

69
00:05:02.742 --> 00:05:05.181
"That's what?" Cole asked.

70
00:05:05.182 --> 00:05:12.420
"It was that little kid, Marty Martin!" Henry exclaimed. "He's our thief!"

71
00:05:12.421 --> 00:05:18.553
"Are you crazy?" Maggie said. "How could Marty be the thief?"

72
00:05:18.554 --> 00:05:23.200
"Yeah," Cole agreed. "Marty is only three years old.

73
00:05:23.201 --> 00:05:25.591
He doesn't even know what money is yet!"

74
00:05:25.592 --> 00:05:30.971
"It doesn't matter." Henry grinned, certain that he was right this time.

75
00:05:30.972 --> 00:05:36.831
"He probably doesn't know what a microphone is either, and Nora just said he took hers.

76
00:05:36.832 --> 00:05:43.692
Now come on, guys. Let's go get Maggie's money back!"

